  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "about": "Names of places outside India and of other cultures, by which a live-research write-back is told to be about somewhere other than an Indian craft (decisions 0135 and 0136). Countries are the member and observer states of the United Nations, with Taiwan, Kosovo, Somaliland and Northern Cyprus, other than India, under their English short names, the names Natural Earth's admin-0 sovereignty layer gives them and the adjectives English uses for them; a test holds every sovereign name of that layer (places_abroad.natural_earth.json) to a country here or to leftOut. Regions and cultures are those that craft, ceramics, textile and metal literature names. leftOut lists the names left out on purpose, each with the Indian sense that keeps it out. Other senses are the names a place word takes inside a material, colour, knot or finish (china clay, Turkey red, German silver) or a sea that washes India (the Arabian Sea); a place word inside one of them names no place abroad. Kept by hand: a write-back refused for a word used in another sense is a reason to add another sense or leave the name out, with a line in the decision log.",
